and I'll be
seeing her around.

526
00:30:36,970 --> 00:30:38,872
Come on, dude,
let's get out of here.

527
00:30:46,781 --> 00:30:47,615
Hey, Quinn.

528
00:30:47,981 --> 00:30:49,083
It's been a minute.

529
00:30:50,017 --> 00:30:51,118
♪ Let me tell you ♪

530
00:30:51,285 --> 00:30:52,886
Are you fucking kidding me?

531
00:30:54,355 --> 00:30:57,592
♪ I have all the reasons
to hate him ♪

532
00:30:57,726 --> 00:30:58,660
Wait.

533
00:30:58,793 --> 00:30:59,893
♪ But you know what? ♪

534
00:31:00,027 --> 00:31:02,029
Dude. Who the fuck
is the new girl?

535
00:31:02,831 --> 00:31:03,931
It's Max.

536
00:31:04,833 --> 00:31:06,066
Where'd you get the pizza?

537
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:07,769
♪ Feels like this,
feels like this ♪

538
00:31:08,135 --> 00:31:09,236
It's true.

539
00:31:09,403 --> 00:31:10,237
It's true.

540
00:31:10,839 --> 00:31:12,239
Everybody's thinking it.

541
00:31:12,473 --> 00:31:13,775
[laughing]

542
00:31:14,441 --> 00:31:15,844
Oh, guys,
Quinn's coming this way

543
00:31:15,976 --> 00:31:17,444
and she looks pissed.

544
00:31:18,011 --> 00:31:18,946
Shit.

545
00:31:19,547 --> 00:31:20,981
I want to go back
to the video store.

546
00:31:21,115 --> 00:31:22,082
Excuse me.

547
00:31:22,950 --> 00:31:23,984
Now.

548
00:31:24,586 --> 00:31:25,386
Quinn.

549
00:31:27,589 --> 00:31:28,723
♪ You're done ♪

550
00:31:28,857 --> 00:31:30,023
♪ Don't go ♪

551
00:31:30,157 --> 00:31:31,291
You guys didn't tell
her I was coming?

552
00:31:31,425 --> 00:31:32,794
Not really.

553
00:31:32,926 --> 00:31:34,361
We wanted it to be a surprise.

554
00:31:34,495 --> 00:31:37,030
Well, fuck, Dan! The only
surprise is that your brain

555
00:31:37,164 --> 00:31:39,166
doesn't fall out your ass
when you take a shit!

556
00:31:39,333 --> 00:31:40,668
[Big Dan] How is this my fault?

557
00:31:40,802 --> 00:31:41,603
[Max] Argh!

558
00:31:41,736 --> 00:31:42,903
♪ Stop laughing ♪

559
00:31:43,705 --> 00:31:44,938
♪ Stop crying ♪

560
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:47,408
♪ Don't do anything ♪

561
00:31:48,710 --> 00:31:51,278
[Radio]...pizza, the best pies
in Carpenter Falls.

562
00:31:51,412 --> 00:31:53,247
Carryout or delivery available.

563
00:31:53,380 --> 00:31:54,314
Oh, hi.

564
00:31:55,949 --> 00:31:58,787
Oh. Into the scary stuff, huh?

565
00:31:59,052 --> 00:32:01,121
Yeah. I can't wait
to watch these.

566
00:32:01,790 --> 00:32:04,992
Yeah, my granddaughter
loves these, too.

567
00:32:05,827 --> 00:32:07,127
This stuff doesn't scare you?

568
00:32:07,394 --> 00:32:08,929
That's kind of the point.

569
00:32:09,764 --> 00:32:11,432
Point taken.

570
00:32:12,132 --> 00:32:14,134
Uh. Let's see.

571
00:32:14,536 --> 00:32:15,335
Here we go.

572
00:32:16,136 --> 00:32:17,605
- There you go.
- Thank you.

573
00:32:17,739 --> 00:32:20,742
Oh, well, thank you, sir.
And... be safe.

574
00:32:20,875 --> 00:32:22,109
I will. Thanks.

575
00:32:22,510 --> 00:32:25,145
- Thank you.
- You bet. Bye.

576
00:32:27,014 --> 00:32:28,081
[sighs]

577
00:32:31,018 --> 00:32:32,119
Okay.

578
00:32:32,654 --> 00:32:36,323
You've been looking
at this shelf for a while now.

579
00:32:36,457 --> 00:32:39,326
There something I can help you
find before we have to close?

580
00:32:39,460 --> 00:32:41,696
Sorry. Just a little indecisive.

581
00:32:41,830 --> 00:32:43,565
No problem. Let me see.

582
00:32:44,566 --> 00:32:49,303
You strike me as a man who
loves action and horror,

583
00:32:49,436 --> 00:32:52,406
but only horror
if it's story driven.

584
00:32:53,207 --> 00:32:55,543
Oh. Don't ask. It's a gift.

585
00:32:56,511 --> 00:32:57,311
Um,

586
00:32:58,713 --> 00:33:00,180
this is the one for you.

587
00:33:00,949 --> 00:33:01,783
Right on the money.

588
00:33:01,916 --> 00:33:03,918
Mhm. Solid story.

589
00:33:04,051 --> 00:33:08,523
Really thrilling action
sequences and good suspense.

590
00:33:08,857 --> 00:33:11,693
And the actors
that play the couple?

591
00:33:11,826 --> 00:33:13,460
Really great chemistry.

592
00:33:14,027 --> 00:33:15,262
Well I'm sold.

593
00:33:15,964 --> 00:33:17,064
Check it out.

594
00:33:18,967 --> 00:33:20,000
Is it a love story?

595
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,569
Oh, I think you'll dig it.

596
00:33:22,570 --> 00:33:24,973
Okay, we're heading to a
cabin with some friends.

597
00:33:25,105 --> 00:33:26,574
Figured we'd pick
something up, so.

598
00:33:26,975 --> 00:33:28,008
- Yeah.
- Fine.

599
00:33:28,275 --> 00:33:29,476
We're good?

600
00:33:29,844 --> 00:33:31,946
This is what the lady says.
I think we should listen.

601
00:33:32,279 --> 00:33:34,214
All right.
I'll catch you at the counter.

602
00:33:34,582 --> 00:33:36,518
- Finally. Thank you.
- Shut up.

603
00:33:38,887 --> 00:33:40,522
[foreboding music]

604
00:33:44,024 --> 00:33:46,026
I promise you.
I'll be gentle.

605
00:33:48,061 --> 00:33:50,063
[bar chatter]

606
00:33:55,068 --> 00:33:56,203
[tv] After her!

607
00:34:10,018 --> 00:34:11,151
[Jojo] Remind me again.

608
00:34:11,653 --> 00:34:12,854
Why am I here?

609
00:34:13,053 --> 00:34:15,088
[Cooper] Because you suck
at fending off peer pressure.

610
00:34:15,422 --> 00:34:18,058
Those lesbians have me
so fucking pissed off.

611
00:34:18,893 --> 00:34:21,763
I just need to release some
of this pent up frustration.

612
00:34:24,131 --> 00:34:25,533
Do you ever wonder
what it's like?

613
00:34:25,967 --> 00:34:26,768
[Cooper] What?

614
00:34:26,901 --> 00:34:28,068
Hook up with a dude?

615
00:34:28,903 --> 00:34:30,004
Why would you think that?

616
00:34:30,137 --> 00:34:31,238
Are you some sort of fag?

617
00:34:31,371 --> 00:34:32,239
- No!
- Hey.

618
00:34:32,372 --> 00:34:33,508
Hey, eyes up here.

619
00:34:33,675 --> 00:34:35,208
You better not be
checking out my ass.

620
00:34:35,475 --> 00:34:36,276
Go!

621
00:34:43,585 --> 00:34:46,186
[Jojo] Sorry, bucko.
We didn't see you there.

622
00:34:49,289 --> 00:34:50,457
Oh, shit.

623
00:34:50,625 --> 00:34:52,392
He's digging up
that Marilyn Miller.

624
00:34:53,093 --> 00:34:54,361
Hey.

625
00:34:54,494 --> 00:34:55,763
What the hell do you
think you're doing here?

626
00:34:56,263 --> 00:34:57,865
[Cooper] I'm talking to you,
Chewbacca.

627
00:35:01,168 --> 00:35:02,870
[tense music]

628
00:35:09,978 --> 00:35:11,311
- [thud]
- [Cooper groans]

629
00:35:11,646 --> 00:35:13,313
[dramatic music]

630
00:35:14,949 --> 00:35:16,483
[squelch]

631
00:35:17,284 --> 00:35:19,219
[blood spurting]

632
00:35:23,891 --> 00:35:25,258
No! No!

633
00:35:26,426 --> 00:35:28,462
[Cooper] Leave me alone!
I want to go home!

634
00:35:31,966 --> 00:35:32,800
No!

635
00:35:33,034 --> 00:35:35,570
No! Just want to go home!

636
00:35:36,738 --> 00:35:38,506
[groaning]

637
00:35:38,906 --> 00:35:40,642
[screaming]

638
00:35:43,911 --> 00:35:45,647
[screaming]

639
00:35:49,149 --> 00:35:50,585
[screaming]

640
00:36:08,536 --> 00:36:10,872
[haunting vocalizing]

641
00:36:26,654 --> 00:36:28,890
[ominous, dramatic music]

642
00:36:48,576 --> 00:36:54,214
Twisted Turbo,
available everywhere, now!

643
00:36:56,150 --> 00:36:59,187
Welcome back to late night
horror theater.

644
00:36:59,453 --> 00:37:01,556
[woman screaming on tv]

645
00:37:04,158 --> 00:37:05,492
[Man] Woo!

646
00:37:10,464 --> 00:37:11,899
[knocking]

647
00:37:13,201 --> 00:37:18,405
So I guess our plan didn't go
as well as we all had hoped?

648
00:37:19,406 --> 00:37:20,575
You knew about this?

649
00:37:22,210 --> 00:37:24,145
I might have had a hand in it.

650
00:37:24,779 --> 00:37:26,748
Unbelievable.
I can't trust anybody.

651
00:37:26,914 --> 00:37:30,618
Hey, we all just want
what's best for you.

652
00:37:30,885 --> 00:37:33,821
You think someone abandoning
me is what's best for me?

653
00:37:34,655 --> 00:37:36,624
Okay, Moody Blues.

654
00:37:37,892 --> 00:37:40,427
I understand why
you're angry at Max.

655
00:37:40,561 --> 00:37:43,831
It was shitty how
she just took up and left.

656
00:37:43,965 --> 00:37:46,968
But give her an
opportunity to explain.

657
00:37:47,467 --> 00:37:48,569
Why should I?

658
00:37:49,804 --> 00:37:50,705
Quinn.

659
00:37:52,372 --> 00:37:54,709
you don't have
to pretend with me.

660
00:37:55,777 --> 00:37:58,579
I saw how close
the two of you were.

661
00:37:59,514 --> 00:38:01,949
Okay, well, her leaving
negated any feelings.

662
00:38:02,083 --> 00:38:05,452
Okay? Why can't she just
tell me why she did it?

663
00:38:07,387 --> 00:38:11,458
If I could play devil's
advocate here for just a minute.

664
00:38:12,093 --> 00:38:13,828
I remember both of you

665
00:38:14,028 --> 00:38:17,497
dreaming of a life outside
of Carpenter Falls.

666
00:38:18,132 --> 00:38:20,400
Well, some of us have
responsibilities.

667
00:38:20,968 --> 00:38:22,503
Oh, honey, please.

668
00:38:23,037 --> 00:38:25,106
Please. You mean you want
to live with this old broad

669
00:38:25,239 --> 00:38:27,909
and run a video store
the rest of your life?

670
00:38:28,042 --> 00:38:28,910
Come on, Grandma.

671
00:38:31,179 --> 00:38:33,014
All I'm saying is just...

672
00:38:34,982 --> 00:38:37,685
don't make a decision
out of anger.

673
00:38:39,352 --> 00:38:41,689
Those usually can't be undone.

674
00:38:54,936 --> 00:38:57,404
Can't play it safe
all your life, sweetie.

675
00:39:09,984 --> 00:39:11,586
[exhales]

676
00:39:16,991 --> 00:39:18,960
[foreboding music]

677
00:39:50,224 --> 00:39:51,926
Well, somebody missed out.

678
00:39:52,059 --> 00:39:54,896
Last night's Grave Rave
was a smash hit.

679
00:39:55,029 --> 00:39:55,596
Great!

680
00:39:55,863 --> 00:39:57,365
There are so many ways

681
00:39:57,497 --> 00:40:00,334
we can capitalize on the legacy
of Marilyn Lee Miller.

682
00:40:00,467 --> 00:40:02,103
And this is just the beginning!

683
00:40:02,603 --> 00:40:03,771
I'm thinking we should
do something

684
00:40:03,905 --> 00:40:05,539
with the old Miller property.

685
00:40:05,673 --> 00:40:08,009
I mean, look what Graceland has
done for the city of Memphis.

686
00:40:08,276 --> 00:40:10,845
Millions and millions
in added tax revenue.

687
00:40:11,178 --> 00:40:13,347
International
tourist destination.

688
00:40:13,981 --> 00:40:15,383
I'm thinking that old property

689
00:40:15,516 --> 00:40:17,985
could be Carpenter Falls'
Graceland.

690
00:40:18,586 --> 00:40:22,189
Looks like you've got it all
figured out, Mayor Bloomberg.

691
00:40:22,323 --> 00:40:23,724
Well, yeah.

692
00:40:23,858 --> 00:40:25,092
I mean, people from all over
would come to experience

693
00:40:25,226 --> 00:40:27,728
the rich history
of a silver screen legend.

694
00:40:27,862 --> 00:40:29,230
And you know what that means?

695
00:40:29,429 --> 00:40:30,364
Thank you.

696
00:40:30,497 --> 00:40:31,866
Do you know what that means?

697
00:40:32,066 --> 00:40:33,834
That means that your little
video store over here

698
00:40:33,968 --> 00:40:35,736
could experience
big business, too.

699
00:40:35,870 --> 00:40:38,039
Oh, well, that would
be interesting.

700
00:40:38,172 --> 00:40:39,707
Yes. Very interesting.

701
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,676
Yeah, I agree, I'm about to
go over to Julia's right now

702
00:40:41,809 --> 00:40:43,077
and work out all the details.

703
00:40:43,210 --> 00:40:45,279
This town needs
a boost like this!

704
00:40:45,746 --> 00:40:47,648
- [phone vibrating]
- Excuse me.

705
00:40:47,882 --> 00:40:49,984
My cellular phone is vibrating.

706
00:40:51,185 --> 00:40:51,986
Bloomberg.

707
00:40:53,254 --> 00:40:54,121
Hey, Alice.

708
00:40:55,122 --> 00:40:55,990
Yeah.

709
00:40:57,425 --> 00:40:59,026
What do you mean,
at the cemetery?

710
00:41:01,395 --> 00:41:02,730
They found what?

711
00:41:03,931 --> 00:41:04,832
Oh, God.

712
00:41:09,870 --> 00:41:11,572
I feel so bad for Logan Miller.

713
00:41:12,239 --> 00:41:13,941
Shit. Show of a family
and now guys like that

714
00:41:14,075 --> 00:41:16,410
are trying to capitalize
on his tragedy.

715
00:41:16,544 --> 00:41:17,477
It's fucked up.

716
00:41:17,979 --> 00:41:20,748
Yeah, well, screw Bloomberg.

717
00:41:21,248 --> 00:41:22,717
He's a slimeball.

718
00:41:29,489 --> 00:41:31,025
[door bell rings]

719
00:41:31,993 --> 00:41:34,862
[rock music plays on radio]

720
00:41:38,432 --> 00:41:40,167
Open heart, open mind.

721
00:41:45,072 --> 00:41:45,906
[Beka] Hey, babe.

722
00:41:46,307 --> 00:41:47,174
Hey.

723
00:41:47,375 --> 00:41:48,342
Are you okay?

724
00:41:48,642 --> 00:41:50,711
We are so sorry.

725
00:41:51,012 --> 00:41:52,713
We just care about you, and...

726
00:41:53,247 --> 00:41:55,016
we wanted to do something
nice for you.

727
00:41:55,383 --> 00:41:56,217
I get it.

728
00:41:57,385 --> 00:41:59,320
Um, yeah. No. I'm sorry.

729
00:41:59,453 --> 00:42:01,288
I kind of flipped my shit
on you guys last night.

730
00:42:01,455 --> 00:42:05,326
So does that mean you don't
want to kill us anymore?

731
00:42:05,793 --> 00:42:07,395
- I think so.
- Quinn?

732
00:42:07,528 --> 00:42:10,564
I just want you to know I had
nothing to do with their plan.

733
00:42:10,698 --> 00:42:12,233
I'm sorry they're stupid.

734
00:42:14,001 --> 00:42:14,869
Anyways.

735
00:42:15,803 --> 00:42:17,772
We messed things up
big time, and--

736
00:42:17,905 --> 00:42:20,174
No, listen. I get it, okay?

737
00:42:20,741 --> 00:42:21,976
It was-

738
00:42:23,110 --> 00:42:25,980
It was a lot of different
emotions, that's all.

739
00:42:26,247 --> 00:42:27,048
But I'll be fine.

740
00:42:27,815 --> 00:42:28,916
You say that a lot.

741
00:42:29,150 --> 00:42:30,851
Like a whole lot.

742
00:42:31,419 --> 00:42:32,987
But we still love you.

743
00:42:33,721 --> 00:42:36,924
And... so does Max.

744
00:42:37,858 --> 00:42:39,960
[tender music]

745
00:42:40,327 --> 00:42:41,162
Where is she?

746
00:43:04,618 --> 00:43:05,686
[Max] If it makes a difference,

747
00:43:05,820 --> 00:43:07,354
I thought you knew I was coming.

748
00:43:09,256 --> 00:43:10,124
I thought...

749
00:43:12,293 --> 00:43:14,161
I thought you wanted me
to be here.

750
00:43:25,973 --> 00:43:27,341
Where did you go, Max?

751
00:43:29,110 --> 00:43:32,246
You just- you left,
and you didn't tell anyone.

752
00:43:32,581 --> 00:43:34,115
I couldn't say anything.

753
00:43:35,517 --> 00:43:36,350
Why not?

754
00:43:37,218 --> 00:43:38,619
Because...

755
00:43:41,489 --> 00:43:43,124
because it was easier that way.

756
00:43:43,691 --> 00:43:45,059
Yeah, easier for you.

757
00:43:45,826 --> 00:43:47,529
It wasn't easy for me. I-

758
00:43:47,661 --> 00:43:50,464
I needed you.
I needed my best friend.

759
00:43:50,631 --> 00:43:51,665
You're right.

760
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:55,102
I should have told you.

761
00:43:57,238 --> 00:44:00,741
I just wanted to be free of
this place and all the bullshit.

762
00:44:03,811 --> 00:44:05,246
I'm sorry, Quinny.

763
00:44:09,817 --> 00:44:12,720
I guess it is kind of cool,
seeing you.

764
00:44:14,788 --> 00:44:16,290
It's good to see you, too.

765
00:44:17,992 --> 00:44:19,793
I'm sorry I went nuclear on you.

766
00:44:20,694 --> 00:44:22,062
You deserved it, but...

767
00:44:22,631 --> 00:44:24,798
I shouldn't have gone off
on a friend like that.

768
00:44:25,132 --> 00:44:26,033
Ah.

769
00:44:27,636 --> 00:44:29,170
I see.

770
00:44:30,871 --> 00:44:32,173
A friend.

771
00:44:33,575 --> 00:44:34,975
Yeah. You're my oldest friend.

772
00:44:36,877 --> 00:44:38,547
Yeah. To be honest, Quinn,

773
00:44:39,548 --> 00:44:42,816
that was one of the reasons
I had to go.

774
00:44:44,752 --> 00:44:48,822
Being your friend, it wasn't
enough for me anymore.

775
00:44:50,024 --> 00:44:53,227
Yeah, well, I don't know
if I was- or if I'm...

776
00:44:57,131 --> 00:45:00,501
I mean, you have never
had a problem

777
00:45:00,635 --> 00:45:02,136
being who you are, and...

778
00:45:03,505 --> 00:45:04,705
for me,

779
00:45:05,607 --> 00:45:08,510
I'm being all of these different
things for different people,

780
00:45:08,643 --> 00:45:09,843
and I'm tired.

781
00:45:10,545 --> 00:45:14,114
And I just don't have the energy
to be who I need to be for me.

782
00:45:16,250 --> 00:45:21,055
You'd be surprised who and what
I have a problem being.

783
00:45:23,224 --> 00:45:25,726
You're stronger than you
give yourself credit for.

784
00:45:30,064 --> 00:45:31,799
[mellow music]

785
00:45:31,999 --> 00:45:34,468
♪ Messed up, you are ♪

786
00:45:34,603 --> 00:45:35,803
[Erin] They are holding hands.

787
00:45:36,003 --> 00:45:37,606
♪ Like I'm Yoda ♪

788
00:45:38,305 --> 00:45:41,976
♪ You wish we aren't
good company ♪

